   "user_message": "Given our goal of reaching £20k MRR within 12 months while keeping monthly churn under 4%, should we increase the Pro plan price from £49 to £59 per month with the next Pro feature release?",
   "assistant_message": "I’ve mapped the price-rise decision, but the first pass cannot answer it yet.\n\nThe arithmetic still answers part of this. If MRR is Pro plan price × Pro paying subscribers (Olumi’s reading of your goal): at 49 £/month and 250 Pro paying subscribers (Olumi’s estimate), MRR is 12,250 £/month today. At 59 £/month, MRR stays at least that while 208 or more of the 250 stay (a loss of at most 42). At 54 £/month (Olumi’s estimate), MRR stays at least that while 227 or more of the 250 stay (a loss of at most 23). 20,000 £/month needs 339 at 59 £/month, 371 at 54 £/month or 409 at 49 £/month. This is arithmetic on these figures, not the analysis ranking the options, and it says nothing about how many will stay.\n\n- Your £49 and proposed £59 prices are recorded; churn must stay below 4%.\n- This is a provisional model using Olumi estimates for subscribers, churn, and new subscriptions.\n- It needs your current MRR and confirmation of how MRR is calculated.\n\n“Olumi reads ‘MRR’ as ‘Pro plan price’ × ‘Pro paying subscribers’, less ‘MRR lost to price resistance’. Is that how you work it out?” Please confirm on the button.\n\nThis run doesn’t show how often each option reaches the goal’s target. Olumi reads 'MRR' as 'Pro plan price' × 'Pro paying subscribers', but that hasn't been confirmed, so this run gives no chance of reaching the target for 'MRR'.\n\nThis model doesn't yet say whether any option gets there within 12 months.\n\nWhat I proposed above is not made until you approve it. Questions this model does not answer yet: Does \"MRR\" get there within 12 months? The model holds the deadline; no result answers that yet. Olumi reads \"MRR\" as depending on \"Pro plan price\" times \"Pro paying subscribers\". 9 more questions remain unresolved."
  },
